# Fault approx_bound (writer 6): crps(gx[i] weight gw[i] for i in g, y0), each gw[i] a `pdf(...) to 1e-30`, printed an
# exact fraction. L §7.3 The error bound: "A printed result that rests on rounded transcendentals, with no round after
# them, prints ≈ and a bound on its distance from the true real-number value"; L §5.18 Output: "A value that rests on a
# correctly rounded transcendental prints ≈ and its error bound". The line asserts the ≈ form only (its digits are the
# interpreter's interval arithmetic over L §5.15's formula).
=== p18.tally
model p18
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

source s "synthetic"

index g = int 1..3

input gx[i in g]: num
input y0: num

def gw[i in g]: num = pdf(normal(0, 1), gx[i]) to 1e-30

ask q: crps(gx[i] weight gw[i] for i in g, y0) law 2026-01-31 orient lower

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  gx[1] = -1 "row"
  gx[2] = 0 "row"
  gx[3] = 1 "row"
  y0 = 0.5 "row"
=== expect
q: ≈ ...
  law date 2026-01-31, cut 2026-01-31
  orient lower
